# A thread open in a BACKGROUND tab: Pin from its sidebar row pins the thread,
# keeps the tab (preview -> kept, into the pinned prefix) and SELECTS it -- a
# pin says you are keeping this thread, the promotion a click into a preview
# makes (the reference's setThreadPinned does the same). Unpin never selects:
# with t2 in front again, Unpin on t9's row leaves t2 in front. Rows are
# anchored by id: "kicker-tick" is t9's row title AND its tab label while the
# tab is open, and a text anchor could land on either.
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2","t9"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
require_thread t2
wait_frames 12
expect_open t2
expect_tab t9 kept

right_click_ui chat_row_id_t9
wait_frames 8
click_ui row_menu_pin
wait_frames 16
expect_starred t9 yes
expect_tab t9 pinned
expect_open t9

click_ui tab_t2
wait_frames 12
expect_open t2

right_click_ui chat_row_id_t9
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Unpin"
click_ui row_menu_pin
wait_frames 16
expect_starred t9 no
expect_tab t9 unpinned
expect_open t2
